From: Aspartame GTK4 migration
Subject: [PATCH] home: expose Activity icons to accessibility clients

GTK4 Home Activity icons are custom Sugar widgets, so they do not inherit a
useful accessible name automatically. Give each icon a button role while
retaining Sugar's custom rendering and activation behavior.

---
 src/jarabe/desktop/favoritesview.py | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/jarabe/desktop/favoritesview.py b/src/jarabe/desktop/favoritesview.py
--- a/src/jarabe/desktop/favoritesview.py
+++ b/src/jarabe/desktop/favoritesview.py
@@ -374,6 +374,10 @@ class ActivityIcon(CanvasIcon):
         CanvasIcon.__init__(self, cache=True,
                             file_name=activity_info.get_icon())

+        self.set_focusable(True)
+        self.update_property([Gtk.AccessibleProperty.LABEL],
+                             [activity_info.get_name()])
+        self.set_accessible_role(Gtk.AccessibleRole.BUTTON)
